Package: zuarrow
Title: Exact Conversion Between R Vectors and 'Apache Arrow' Columns
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Pedro", "Baltazar", , "pedrobtz@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("The Apache Software Foundation", role = "cph",
           comment = "nanoarrow, bundled in src/vendor/nanoarrow"),
    person("Mikkel F.", "Jørgensen", role = "cph",
           comment = "flatcc runtime, bundled in src/vendor/nanoarrow"),
    person("Paul", "Hsieh", role = "cph",
           comment = "pstdint.h in the bundled flatcc runtime"))
Description: Moves columns between R and the 'Apache Arrow' columnar
    format: the C data interface in memory and the inter-process
    communication ('IPC') stream and file formats on disk. Every 'Arrow'
    type converts to an R vector and back, and a conversion either keeps
    every value unchanged or raises an error that names the column and the
    R type that would hold it exactly. A registry lets other packages
    declare which R class is the exact form of which 'Arrow' type. Handles
    share the layout of the 'nanoarrow' package, so objects pass between
    the two without conversion. The bundled 'nanoarrow' C library
    (<https://github.com/apache/arrow-nanoarrow>) needs no system library.
    The format is specified at
    <https://arrow.apache.org/docs/format/Columnar.html>.
